(1405266, 178902, 38152, '<td valign="top">Wow!  The bubbles are so clear and the water by the apple has such a glassy sheen...brrr...I can feel my toes getting wet and cold reaching for that apple!  I like the contrast between the red, white and black.  I also like the off center focal point and the multiple textures...just enough for the simplicity of the picture so that it draws your viewer in without becoming over stimulated.  Nice job!</td>', 'Wow!  The bubbles are so clear and the water by the apple has such a glassy sheen...brrr...I can feel my toes getting wet and cold reaching for that apple!  I like the contrast between the red, white and black.  I also like the off center focal point and the multiple textures...just enough for the simplicity of the picture so that it draws your viewer in without becoming over stimulated.  Nice job!', '2005-05-23 02:41:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1405290, 179218, 38152, '<td valign="top">I LOVE IT!  The crispness of the snail and grass are fabulous.  The vertical lines in the head of the snail flow with the vertical lines of the apple and grass while the disorderly horizontal blades of grass, the stripes on the snails shell, and the blurred horizontal lines of the structure in the background are subtle but intricate contrasts that have made this photo fantastic!  I enjoyed the true presence of texture which draws your viewer into this clever picture.  I also enjoyed that only a few hues were made present in this entire picture which are blended spledidly  but adds a touch of something familiar for the viewer.  A pure pleasure to look at.  Your title is adorable as well!  Great work.</td>', 'I LOVE IT!  The crispness of the snail and grass are fabulous.  The vertical lines in the head of the snail flow with the vertical lines of the apple and grass while the disorderly horizontal blades of grass, the stripes on the snails shell, and the blurred horizontal lines of the structure in the background are subtle but intricate contrasts that have made this photo fantastic!  I enjoyed the true presence of texture which draws your viewer into this clever picture.  I also enjoyed that only a few hues were made present in this entire picture which are blended spledidly  but adds a touch of something familiar for the viewer.  A pure pleasure to look at.  Your title is adorable as well!  Great work.', '2005-05-23 02:56:55.000000', NULL, 1),
