(1410173, 179327, 28695, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments and, as a number of people realized, I don''t speak German (at least not well nor since high school).  I just liked the German word for apple (Apfel) and the title just kinda took on a life of its own.  Believe me, I got a great deal of personal amusement coming up with the title.  After voting started, I realized that "wohnen" (to dwell) was not the word I was thinking of, but I was thinking of "weissen" (to know).  I even got the umlaut wrong.  Sigh.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments and, as a number of people realized, I don''t speak German (at least not well nor since high school).  I just liked the German word for apple (Apfel) and the title just kinda took on a life of its own.  Believe me, I got a great deal of personal amusement coming up with the title.  After voting started, I realized that "wohnen" (to dwell) was not the word I was thinking of, but I was thinking of "weissen" (to know).  I even got the umlaut wrong.  Sigh.', '2005-05-25 01:14:40.000000', NULL, 0),
