(1410860, 178366, 22559, '<td valign="top">Thanks all for comments. :)</td>', 'Thanks all for comments. :)', '2005-05-25 07:47:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(1410863, 177702, 649, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone who voted and commented.  No real photoshop trick here.  It was done with a mini flashlight and a 30 second exposure.</td>', 'Thanks to everyone who voted and commented.  No real photoshop trick here.  It was done with a mini flashlight and a 30 second exposure.', '2005-05-25 07:50:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(1410864, 177953, 36521, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sibeling:</b></div><hr/><i> This is definitely interesting, but the focus is quite soft, and I find myself trying to figure out what the setting is, rather than enjoying viewing the apple. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I guess the focus was kinda soft because the first apple that you see in the picture is actually the reflection of the original apple which is not in the picture.  Because if I had the focus on the original apple, I won''t be able to capture the effect of the reflection of the mirror.<br/> <br/>Thanks for your vote :o)</td>', 'Originally posted by sibeling: This is definitely interesting, but the focus is quite soft, and I find myself trying to figure out what the setting is, rather than enjoying viewing the apple.   I guess the focus was kinda soft because the first apple that you see in the picture is actually the reflection of the original apple which is not in the picture.  Because if I had the focus on the original apple, I won''t be able to capture the effect of the reflection of the mirror. Thanks for your vote :o)', '2005-05-25 07:50:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(1410868, 177953, 36521, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by itsgodswork:</b></div><hr/><i> could u blured out the rest of apples. i would love it. but this is a top top-20 photo. possibly a ribbon photo. but this is definatley a print avaible photo. the oother apples are quite distracting but i give you a 9 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks :o) even if your prediction didn''t happen :o)</td>', 'Originally posted by itsgodswork: could u blured out the rest of apples. i would love it. but this is a top top-20 photo. possibly a ribbon photo. but this is definatley a print avaible photo. the oother apples are quite distracting but i give you a 9   Thanks :o) even if your prediction didn''t happen :o)', '2005-05-25 07:53:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1410878, 177953, 36521, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all who posted comments and voted on this one :o)</td>', 'Thanks to all who posted comments and voted on this one :o)', '2005-05-25 07:59:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1410887, 177452, 30018, '<td valign="top">This is sad, that this image finished so low in the challenge.  I had hoped for a top 10!  This is a beautiful image.  One of my favs!</td>', 'This is sad, that this image finished so low in the challenge.  I had hoped for a top 10!  This is a beautiful image.  One of my favs!', '2005-05-25 08:05:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1410894, 179309, 27482, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by insane:</b></div><hr/><i> I see from, what you wrote, that you do many water shot''s and that you are particulary interested in this theme. <br/></i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I don´t really see where you get this idea, as I clearly stated in the photographers comments I say "This is my first time doing anything similiar as this and it was a lot of fun, I am definately going to do this again sometime."<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by insane:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>Don''t get me wrong, but  I am infuriated, that people spray objects with water drops or use some water techniques, since it''s seems to me so cheap.Well we know that there are loads of water shot''s in here so I say we should try to do something invoative. For some time now I am discriminating all water shots. It''s just that there were some really impresive ideas and they where executed in a very good way. Your shot is just not a ribbond winner. It''s not a symbol of an ''ideal or the best'' image to me.<br/></i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well fair enough, that is your opinion but you can never please everybody and while I appreciate your opinion on this, I respectfully disagree.  I don´t think there has ever been a ribbon winner here at DPC that doesn´t get a lot of 4 and less in grades so there you go.  I must admit though that several times I have given ribbon winnners "low" scores so all I can say is that fortunately different people have different tastes and it all pretty much evens out in the end.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by insane:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>Well I can''t say I''m an adulator.  I speak my mind and if I have offended you, then I am sorry, that wasn''t my intention.<br/></i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hehe, don´t worry, none taken, I value people that say their opinions, no matter how much I disagree.<br/> <br/>To everybody, thanx for the comments, favorites and of course the votes, I appreciate it.  Now for the hard part, to get another ribbon to prove I am not a "one hit wonder" :o).  Cheers from Iceland, Larus.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-05-25 07:30:09.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by insane: I see from, what you wrote, that you do many water shot''s and that you are particulary interested in this theme.   I don´t really see where you get this idea, as I clearly stated in the photographers comments I say "This is my first time doing anything similiar as this and it was a lot of fun, I am definately going to do this again sometime." Originally posted by insane: Don''t get me wrong, but  I am infuriated, that people spray objects with water drops or use some water techniques, since it''s seems to me so cheap.Well we know that there are loads of water shot''s in here so I say we should try to do something invoative. For some time now I am discriminating all water shots. It''s just that there were some really impresive ideas and they where executed in a very good way. Your shot is just not a ribbond winner. It''s not a symbol of an ''ideal or the best'' image to me.  Well fair enough, that is your opinion but you can never please everybody and while I appreciate your opinion on this, I respectfully disagree.  I don´t think there has ever been a ribbon winner here at DPC that doesn´t get a lot of 4 and less in grades so there you go.  I must admit though that several times I have given ribbon winnners "low" scores so all I can say is that fortunately different people have different tastes and it all pretty much evens out in the end. Originally posted by insane: Well I can''t say I''m an adulator.  I speak my mind and if I have offended you, then I am sorry, that wasn''t my intention.  Hehe, don´t worry, none taken, I value people that say their opinions, no matter how much I disagree. To everybody, thanx for the comments, favorites and of course the votes, I appreciate it.  Now for the hard part, to get another ribbon to prove I am not a "one hit wonder" :o).  Cheers from Iceland, Larus.', '2005-05-25 08:13:52.000000', '2005-05-25 08:30:09.000000', 0),
(1410900, 179309, 37961, '<td valign="top">Many concepts go into a winning photo. What does it for me is the contrast of colors. I love the greenish hue of the water against the apple. Congrats!</td>', 'Many concepts go into a winning photo. What does it for me is the contrast of colors. I love the greenish hue of the water against the apple. Congrats!', '2005-05-25 08:20:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(1410912, 178438, 18450, '<td valign="top">Awesome first challenge entry Jess. Creative idea and the colours and focus are excellent. I think in this shot I''d love to see the leaves go all the way to the top at the sides, so you can''t see the rocks. <br/> <br/>I like to have fun after the challenges trying different ideas.....with this one I''d try different arrangements of the apple and flowers. Maybe apple off centre or dandelion on top of the apple......stuff like that. It''s such a lovely fresh looking image.</td>', 'Awesome first challenge entry Jess. Creative idea and the colours and focus are excellent. I think in this shot I''d love to see the leaves go all the way to the top at the sides, so you can''t see the rocks.  I like to have fun after the challenges trying different ideas.....with this one I''d try different arrangements of the apple and flowers. Maybe apple off centre or dandelion on top of the apple......stuff like that. It''s such a lovely fresh looking image.', '2005-05-25 08:27:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1410919, 179294, 13365, '<td valign="top">Excellent Shot, Congrats on the 5th!</td>', 'Excellent Shot, Congrats on the 5th!', '2005-05-25 08:28:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(1410929, 177705, 37961, '<td valign="top">I know apple was the theme, but I would love to see this shot with a hat, scarf or something hanging from the fence with a little air movement. Great spot to take pics. Your colors and focus are great.</td>', 'I know apple was the theme, but I would love to see this shot with a hat, scarf or something hanging from the fence with a little air movement. Great spot to take pics. Your colors and focus are great.', '2005-05-25 08:34:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(1410940, 179263, 37851, '<td valign="top">Thank you to everyone for the comments.  This was my first submission, and I will use all the feedback I get to try an improve.</td>', 'Thank you to everyone for the comments.  This was my first submission, and I will use all the feedback I get to try an improve.', '2005-05-25 08:42:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(1410946, 178345, 25095, '<td valign="top">I can''t believe 9th place?!?!?!?!  I gave it a 9 and was totally expecting a ribbon for this one.  At least you got in the top 10.  Great shot with wonderful colors and lighting. Congrats</td>', 'I can''t believe 9th place?!?!?!?!  I gave it a 9 and was totally expecting a ribbon for this one.  At least you got in the top 10.  Great shot with wonderful colors and lighting. Congrats', '2005-05-25 08:44:14.000000', NULL, 0),
