(1412275, 178848, 33899, '<td valign="top">a lot of times the florescent (sp?) lighting messes with the white balance on your camera...that''s why your picture may be tinted blue or red. in this case the camera rendered the picture more along the red side.  keep working on it though, no one wins a ribbon on their first challenge...well, at least not me. :)</td>', 'a lot of times the florescent (sp?) lighting messes with the white balance on your camera...that''s why your picture may be tinted blue or red. in this case the camera rendered the picture more along the red side.  keep working on it though, no one wins a ribbon on their first challenge...well, at least not me. :)', '2005-05-25 18:02:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(1412278, 178969, 33899, '<td valign="top">hmm the flash messed you up.  try either filtering the flash out with some thing opaque sheet over your flash or just try getting yourself a fairly bright white light, like a halogen and then put a lamp cover or something to diffuse the light.</td>', 'hmm the flash messed you up.  try either filtering the flash out with some thing opaque sheet over your flash or just try getting yourself a fairly bright white light, like a halogen and then put a lamp cover or something to diffuse the light.', '2005-05-25 18:04:37.000000', NULL, 0),
